  "T300": "all four V1 points have >= 3 passing runs AND P1 Si 300 AND P1 Ge 300 AND P2 -> endpoint domain restored at 300 K",
  "T700_T1100": "each of 700 K and 1100 K is judged independently: all four points at that T have >= 3 passing runs AND P1 passes for both Si and Ge -> endpoint domain restored at that T",
  "if_condition_fails": "that temperature stays scope-limited; a ledger entry records the failing gate; the negative result is published, not rerun silently",
  "lifts": "scope-limit-alloys-2026-09-27 (endpoint part only, per T)",
  "op": "restore",
  "scope_label": "every restored state carries the label 'Tersoff-1989-parented' plus its measured ratio to the BTE-DFT party (Si 160.5/63.8/40.5, Ge 57.1/25.7/16.7 W/mK at 300/700/1100 K); the ratio is reported, not gating: the gates decide numerical validity of the Tersoff-family number, the label carries its known method bias into every downstream claim"
